        "title": "Managerial Accounting - Decisions, Budgets, Variances",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Managerial accounting is the **forward-looking, internal** discipline that turns the cost\ndata of file 06 into plans (budgets), control (variance analysis), internal pricing\n(transfer pricing), and discrete decisions (relevant costs, capital budgeting). It has no\nGAAP/IFRS rules — its only standard is *usefulness to the decision*. This is the accounting a\nVP with budget responsibility actually operates inside."
    }
